Combine @water{3%cups}, @dry Italian-style salad dressing mix{1%.7 ounce package}, @dried oregano{1%teaspoon}, @dried basil{1%teaspoon}, @dried parsley{1%teaspoon}, @onion salt{1%teaspoon}, @garlic powder{1%teaspoon}, @bay leaf{1}, @salt{1%teaspoon}, and @ground black pepper{1%teaspoon} in a #saucepan{}. Stir well, and bring to a boil.

Place @rump roast{5%pound} in a #slow cooker{}; pour hot herb mixture over the meat.

Cover and cook on Low for ~{10-12%hours}, or on High for ~{4-5%hours}.

Remove bay leaf; shred beef with a fork and serve with some of the hot gravy.